     I just thought I'd mention some things about the idea of a
water_confirm option.  One of the biggest disadvantages would
indoubtedly be the "Omega effect" (Omega has such an option) whereby you
have to hit "y" each time you enter the pool (I don't think typing "yes"
and return is warranted.  People fall in pools so rarely that the chance
of accidentally stepping on a pool and having your modem send "y" at
that moment is miniscule.  Sometimes airtightness isn't worth the
inconvenience).
     It seems to me that checking for levitation and identified boots of
water walking gives the character too much strategical advantage and
lets the game play for the character too much.  However, one *could*
make it so there is no confirm if the character was *previously* on a
water square.  Thus one would only have to confirm once each time he
steps into the water.
     I think it would be neat to have a lake somewhere in the dungeon
that needs to be crossed (the only problem is, I'd think that
teleportability and teleport control would be easier to achieve than
levitation or water walking by that time in the game).

     Just a side-gripe: I note that some items like "leather shoes" can
rust.  ("Your metal boots rust!")  Likewise, "a black cap" doesn't
strike me as being made of metal.
     One item (obviously for 3.1) that I thought would be neat would be
a "fur covering" or something, designed for some type of armor (a
blessed one would fit any type of armor) that would make that type of
armor (e.g. boots, suit, helmet) rustproof.  It could, obviously, be
used only once.  I don't think it would be necessary to code in the
ability to remove it from the armor once applied.

